## 5. Subscription APIs

### 5.1 Create Subscription

**Edge Function**: `create-subscription`

```json
// Request
{
  "campaign_id": "uuid",
  "amount": 500,
  "currency": "INR",
  "donor_name": "Rahul Sharma",
  "donor_email": "rahul@example.com",
  "donor_user_id": "uuid",
  "frequency": "monthly"
}

// Response — Success (200)
{
  "subscription_id": "uuid",
  "razorpay_sub_id": "sub_xxxxxxxxx",
  "amount": 500,
  "status": "active",
  "next_charge_date": "2026-07-12T00:00:00Z"
}

// Response — Error (400)
{ "error": "Campaign is not active." }

// Response — Error (500)
{ "error": "Subscription creation failed." }
```

### 5.2 Cancel Subscription

**Edge Function**: `cancel-subscription`

```json
// Request
{
  "subscription_id": "uuid"
}

// Response — Success (200)
{
  "success": true,
  "cancelled_at": "2026-06-12T14:00:00Z",
  "message": "Subscription cancelled. No future charges will be made."
}

// Response — Error (404)
{ "error": "Subscription not found." }
```

### 5.3 Get Active Subscriptions

```swift
let subscriptions = try await supabase
    .from("subscriptions")
    .select("*, donation_profiles!campaign_id(title, image_url)")
    .eq("user_id", userId)
    .eq("status", "active")
    .execute()
    .value
```

**Auth**: Authenticated (User — own subscriptions via RLS)

### 5.4 Subscription Webhook

**Edge Function**: `subscription-webhook`

```json
// Request (from Razorpay)
{
  "event": "subscription.charged",
  "payload": {
    "subscription": {
      "entity": {
        "id": "sub_xxx",
        "plan_id": "plan_xxx",
        "status": "active",
        "current_start": 1720000000,
        "current_end": 1722678400
      }
    },
    "payment": {
      "entity": {
        "id": "pay_xxx",
        "amount": 50000,
        "status": "captured"
      }
    }
  }
}

// Events Handled:
// - subscription.charged → Create donation record + receipt
// - subscription.payment_failed → Increment retry_count; pause after 3
// - subscription.cancelled → Update subscription status
// - subscription.completed → Update subscription status
```

